title: RecruitReb
position: 26,-338
---
<<set $Blind= true>>
You would imagine contacting such a group would be more difficult, but it turned out to be pretty easy.
Just a matter of cashing in some favours here and there.
The Blind, resided in a small abandoned space station, bound to make an eagle flight of its own in a couple of years.
The once sterile interior was now filled with graffiti and vandalized propaganda. 
The chief of the place, a small framed man with an obviously broken nose and dark slicked back hair, welcomes you with a smile.
???: Salve, the name is Grig, to whom do I owe the pleasure?
->My name's Joh
	Grig: Welcome.
	Now that the presentations are done his face turns less welcoming and more focused. 
	Grig: Why are you here Joh?
		-> I came here to help. I want to help! 
			Grig: You're more than welcome to join our little club, we're always looking to expand here.
			He leans in closer. 
			Grig: But how can you help?	
			-> I can hold a gun.
				The man starts laughing. 
				Grig: That was a fun joke kid.
				Grig: Look at you. You don't look ready to take a life.
				His expression becomes harsh with a sliver of empathy.
				Grig: Not even a Ziemniak's one.
				-> I can do it, sir!
					Grig: Listen, first of all, I'm no one's sir. Just call me Grig. 
					Grig: Secondly are you sure? We can find you some other job on the station.
					-> Yes, I'm sure.
						Grig: Ok then ask Murphy, she will get you up to date. 
						<<set $dadSoldier = true>><<jump Ch2>>
					-> Maybe I should stick to being a mechanic.
						Grig: Good thinking. 
						Grig: We're always in need for good mechanics.
						<<set $dadMech = true>><<jump Ch2>>						
				-> Ehmm I...
					Grig: Listen, we can find you some other job on the station.
					Grig: I don't want you to die kid.
					<<set $dadMech = true>><<jump Ch2>>
			-> I know how to repair machines.
					Grig: Good, We're always in need for good mechanics.
					<<set $dadMech = true>><<jump Ch2>>	
		-> I just wanted to know more about this place.
			Grig: Listen kid. You don't just run into a place like this. 
			His face was as harsh as it could possibly be.
			Grig: Now. You're either with us or not.
			-> I'm here to help sir.
				The man sighs, releasing the tension.
				Grig: Ok then, what can you do? We can indeed find you a job on the station or on the field.
				-> I can hold a gun.
					Grig: Ok then ask Murphy, she will get you up to date. 
					<<set $dadSoldier = true>><<jump Ch2>>
				-> I know how to repair stuff.
					Grig: That's Good, We're always in need for good mechanics.
					<<set $dadMech = true>><<jump Ch2>>	
===
title: Ch2
position: 404,-519
---
<<if $Blind == true>>
	The work was hard, but it came with its rewards. 
	<<if $dadMech == true>>
		Your help was essential in keeping the whole station running.
	<<endif>>
	These people really believed in what they were doing and so did you.
	And they might even have had a shot at creating a free Jovian system. 
	But unfortunately with the treaty that stopped the Shutter, the Blind lost a lot of their supporters.
	That on top of the opening of the Pons and the arrival of both Venuvian and Martian military forces, drove the rebellion to the ground.
<<elseif $Martian == true>>
	Apart from some minor incidents here and there the conflict never exploded into a real war.
	<<if $dadSoldier == true>>
		Your job was mostly containing small uprisings here and there in the system, but not much more. 
	<<elseif $dadMech == true>>
		Your job ended up being fixing and refurbishing old spy drones from earth into full fledged support systems for the inhabitants of the Jovian system.
	<<endif>>
	But luckily those days ended when the Marsuvian alliance managed to secure a successful treaty with Earth. 
	The latter would open back up the water supplies to the Jovian system, and give them partial freedom while remaining in control of the resources on the moons of Europa and Io.
	While Martians and Venuvians would deploy troops in the system to avoid further trouble on Jupiter. 
	Shortly after, the Pons was opened, a neutral station shared between the three forces.
<<endif>>
You would have thought returning to your normal life, would have taken longer. 
But everything moved so fast after those days. And everything felt so weird for some reason.
Not having to worry about water anymore. 
Working as much as possible to rebuild and keep living.
With that lingering anger.
Of knowing all that could have been avoided.
But there are also so many good memories from those years.
There were your friends making you laugh. Sully always causing trouble.
And then there was her. The day you met in Ganymede, your dinners at the Rationale.
Your first appartment, the old sofa where you grew closer. 
Where you hoped you would grow old together.
When Kher was born you two were the happiest people in the Jovian system.
<<if $Blind == true>>
	But soon your ties with the Blind started clashing with your family.
	That kind of life is a risky one, you couldn't keep doing both. 
<<elseif $Martian == true>>
	But soon your duty towards your comrades started clashing with your family.
	The Martians asked you to take long term station for 10 years on an out of system location.
<<endif>> 
	-> Choose duty.
		<<if $Blind == true>>
		You spent the next 5 years working closely with Grig. And you managed to make a difference.
		Thanks to you, the Blind's station turned into a proper base of operation for the group.
		But circumstances changed, and priorities switched.
		When you get the news of her passing, you immediately decide to go back to your life, to your child.
		<<elseif $Martian == true>>
		You spent the next 5 years secretly working on surveillance drones. And you managed to make a difference.
		The money was good and you knew your family was taken care of.
		But sometimes life gets in the way, circumstances changed, and priority switched.
		When you get the news of her passing, you immediately decide to go back to your life, to your child.
		<<endif>> 
		<<if adjust_status(0,1,0,0)>><<endif>>
	-> Choose family.
		The following 5 years are the best of your life. Just the three of you, in the old workshop.
		But sometimes life gets in the way. When she got sick you didn't know how to handle it, but you had to find a way.
		If not for her, for your child. 
		When she passed your life turned gray again.
		<<if adjust_status(0,0,1,0)>><<endif>>
<<jump Ch3>>
===
title: Ch3
position: 641,-656
---
7 years went by in a second. 
You kept working as a mechanic, raising Kher as best you could.
Being a single dad was not always easy. 
But having your own workshop helped with that.
So much that you're even able to have enough time to bring your kid to the orbiting diner, the Rationale.
It took two weeks of annoying you and interrupting you mid work to convince you.
When you went to pick them up from school on Ganymede to finally go there, they looked at you.
Kher: Hey dad, can Kazimierz hang out with us today?
-> No kiddo, today it'll be just the two of us. 
	The calming sound of the ship turning on helped you ignore your kid's upset face. 
	-> so Kher how did it go today? 
		Kher: Ok.
		-> Just drive silently.
		-> Listen kid I know you wanted your friend with us.
			But I really wanted to spend some time just you and me.
			Is that ok? 
			You smiled at them. 
			Kher: I said ok. Don't worry.
		<<jump rational>>
	-> Just silently drive towards the Rationale.
		<<jump rational>>
-> Sure I don't see why not.
	The calming sound of the ship turning on, cover your kid and their friend's chatter.
	<<declare $Hick= true >><<jump rational>>
===
title: rational
---
You arrived at the Rationale. The place was packed full and it took you a minute for them to find you a seat. 
<<if $Hick == true>> 
	The three of you sat in the fake leather chair, while the waitress handed you a menu. 
<<elseif true>>
	The two of you sat in the fake leather chair, while the waitress handed you a menu. 
<<endif>>
You picked it up and read through it.
-> Pick the Barszcz.
	It didn't take you that long to settle on the Barszcz, you always felt more focused after good plate of it.
-> Pick the NutriMix.
	It didn't take you that long to settle on the NutriMix, you always felt stronger after good shake.
-> Pick the Insekczyk.
	It didn't take you that long to settle on the Insekczyk, you can actually find people more tolerable after it.
The evening flew by in a second. 
You found yourself in the ship right outside the workshop. Your kid got out of the ship, while you finished turning down all the systems.
You saw them enter the place and turn on the light.
You were about to switch of the JPS navigation system when you got a message from the integrated log.
<<if $Martian== true>>
	The commander's contact pops up in your messages with a location attached.
	You wonder what job she will have for you this time.
<<elseif $Blind>>
	Grig's contact pops up in your messages with a location attached.
	You wonder what job he will have for you this time.
<<endif>>

-> Go to the location. 
	When you get back home you find the kid sleeping with their book still in their hand.
	Another day has passed.
	<<if adjust_status(0,0,0,1)>><<endif>><<if set_flag("noMessages")>><<endif>>
-> Turn the system down and go back home.
	You got in the house and went to work to finish a project you had been stuck on. 
	Kher decided to help you out, and so the two of you worked together. 
	By the end of the day you tucked them into bed and you knew,
	another day was over.
	<<if adjust_status(1,0,0,0)>><<endif>>
===
title: alphaDialogue
---
Everything is wet when you wake up from cryosleep. 
When you first took the spacecraft to get out of the Jovian system you promised yourself to never go back. 
But here you are, the prodigal child back in their homeland. 

Memories are weird when you wake up from cryo. 

-> Why was I even here? 
	Dad: You were here for me kiddo. 
	You look around but see no one. You shook away the and then remember the message.
	It came by mail what, 6 months ago now? They wrote about your dad's sickness. 
	Dad: Came here to say your final goodbye to your old man?
	Dad: What a lucky father I am.
	-> What's happening?
		Dad: Don't worry about it.
		Then you remember, he is being treated for radiation sickness at Febris hospital in Ganymede. 
	-> What sickness was it again?
		Dad: I don't think it's that important now kiddo.
		Then you remember, he is being treated for radiation sickness at Febris hospital in Ganymede. 
	-> Where is he staying?
		You frantically look through your messages. 
		Six months of spam are a lot to sift through. 
		But here it is... He is being treated for radiation sickness at Febris hospital in Ganymede. 
===